  "details": "It's great that the OS's \"Input Method Editor\" aka IME can now be used for text input on the PICO standalone device, however I am experiencing some accompanying inconveniences.\n\nFirst, when I click on the input field in the Chatbox, the OS's IME will open, which prevents me from clicking and moving the cursor. It would be better to have a \"Open IME\" button.\n\nAdditionally, when I decide to use the traditional VRC soft keyboard instead of opening the OS's IME, the cursor randomly jumps to the beginning of the input field while I'm typing, making it impossible to input text correctly. This happens intermittently.\n\nEven worse, in the Bio's \"Add Note\" feature, pressing Enter in the OS's IME only creates a new line, and It will not close the IME, which prevents me from exiting this edit mode.",
